## table attribute_def | doc="An attribute definition (title, assignee, …). value_type is one of text|number|bool|date|card_ref|card_ref[]. `date` is stored as a JSON string holding an ISO 8601 calendar date ('YYYY-MM-DD'); the predicate compiler's before_today / within_days ops compare these as text (ISO dates sort lexically as chronologically). For card_ref / card_ref[] value_types target_card_type_id names the card_type whose cards are the valid values — that is what unifies every pick-from-a-list attribute (assignee / milestone / component / tag plus any custom card_type a project admin defines): each is a card_ref to value-cards of a specific card_type. There is no enum table and no privileged workflow attribute baked into the schema. target_filter (optional, card_ref / card_ref[] only) is a predicate tree — the screen-filter shape card_compile_predicate compiles — that a card must ALSO satisfy to be chosen as a NEW value: card.search applies it when a picker names the attribute, and attribute.update / card.insert reject a newly chosen card that fails it (values already stored are grandfathered). E.g. assignee offers no contact or disabled person."

### meta
name_column
name

### columns
name, type, pk, unique, nullable, default, references
id, bigserial, true, , , , 
name, text, , true, false, , 
value_type, text, , , false, ,
target_card_type_id, bigint, , , , , card_type.id
is_built_in, boolean, , , false, false,
enum_managed, boolean, , , false, false,
target_filter, jsonb, , , , ,

