## table card | doc="A card instance. phase is a 3-value enum (triage/active/terminal) that categorises flow-bound value-cards used in ref attributes (status='Done' → terminal; status='New idea' → triage; status='Doing' → active). Drives the predicate compiler's has_phase op and the legacy notTerminal alias (phase='terminal'), the TransitionBar UI buckets via (from.phase, to.phase) pairs, and the default-create-status resolution chain. Defaults 'triage' for new value-cards (admins flip to active/terminal at creation time). Cards that are not flow-bound value-cards (tasks, projects, persons, …) carry the default but the value is never consulted. private_to (a person card) makes the card private (docs/PERSONAL_SCREENS.md): visible to and writable by that person's accounts only — their login and its agents, no admin exception — and inherited by cards inserted under it. Watch lists, personal screens and personal views are private; everything else leaves it NULL."

### meta
name_attribute
title

### columns
name, type, pk, nullable, default, references, check
id, bigserial, true, , , ,
card_type_id, bigint, , false, , card_type.id,
parent_card_id, bigint, , , , card.id,
phase, text, , false, 'triage', , "phase IN ('triage','active','terminal')"
created_at, timestamptz, , false, now(), ,
deleted_at, timestamptz, , , , ,
private_to, bigint, , , , card.id,

