## table card_access | doc="Secret routes (docs/MAIL_INTAKE_AND_CALENDARS.md §5): a random token that reaches one card from outside kitp — a calendar feed URL (purpose calendar, card = the calendar), a POST intake URL (inbound_post, card = the comm_channel; provider raw / mailgun / postmark) or an SMTP intake address (inbound_smtp). token_hash is auth.HashSecret of the token (40 lowercase hex characters), which is shown once when the row is made; hint is its first 6 characters, to tell routes apart. comment is the user's label. policy holds a route's filters (sources, require_tls, sender_hosts, envelope_from, header_from, dkim); signing_key is Mailgun's webhook signing key, pgp_sym_encrypt'ed with app.comm_secret_key. last_used_at / last_client / last_error are shown on the page that lists the routes." | unique="token_hash"

### columns
