## function comm_author_join | doc="The author of a message sent from kitp (reply.post, comm.create's initial message) joins comm.comm_recipients: their person, or an agent's owner's person, when it has an email and is missing. Union only, like an inbound sender. Declared before its callers." | path="functions/comm_author_join.sql" | arg_types="bigint, bigint"
## function comm_set_recipients_batch | doc="comm.set_recipients — validate (comm exists, every person_id is a person card) + replace the comm_recipients attribute_value with the deduped, canonicalised list." | path="functions/comm_set_recipients_batch.sql"
## function comm_attach_batch | doc="comm.attach — move a thread onto a task (same project, Tasks on, caller holds task card.update) or back into its project as a thread on its own (task_id 0), keeping the tasks' comms lists in step. Files stay where they are: a thread keeps the files that came by email. See docs/CONVERSATIONS.md." | path="functions/comm_attach_batch.sql"
## function comm_attachment_to_task_batch | doc="comm.attachment_to_task — Add to task: move a file that came by email (it lives on the thread) onto the thread's task, keeping the messages' links; when the task already holds the same bytes the messages link that file and the thread's copy goes, so nothing is stored twice. Caller holds task card.update; Tasks on. See docs/MAIL_INTAKE_AND_CALENDARS.md." | path="functions/comm_attachment_to_task_batch.sql"
## function comm_set_ack_batch | doc="comm.set_ack — validate (comm exists, card_type='comm') + set the per-thread `acked` bool attribute_value (with paired activity row). A received inbound reply clears acked (imap.go); this is the explicit operator acknowledgement that the thread is handled." | path="functions/comm_set_ack_batch.sql"
## function reply_post_batch | doc="reply.post — validate (comm exists, has recipients) + insert reply_body card with 5 attributes (set-based via ordinality join) + append to comm.replies + optional attachment linking." | path="functions/reply_post_batch.sql"
## function person_upsert_by_email_batch | doc="person.upsert_by_email — case-insensitive email match against existing person cards; on miss create a fresh global person card with title / email / person_kind." | path="functions/person_upsert_by_email_batch.sql"
## function flow_set_batch | doc="flow.set — admin-only upsert of one flow row. Validates attribute_def + project scope + optional default_create_status_id target type; maps unique_violation to flow_duplicate_scope." | path="functions/flow_set_batch.sql"
## function flow_delete_batch | doc="flow.delete — admin-only delete of one flow row. Refuses with code='flow_disallowed' and a structured {blockers[], count} payload when any flow_step row still references the flow (admins must clear steps first)." | path="functions/flow_delete_batch.sql"
## function flow_step_set_batch | doc="flow_step.set — admin-only upsert of one flow_step row. Validates flow existence, from/to cards are value-cards of the flow's attribute_def target_card_type, and label uniqueness." | path="functions/flow_step_set_batch.sql"
## function flow_step_delete_batch | doc="flow_step.delete — admin-only delete of one flow_step row by id." | path="functions/flow_step_delete_batch.sql"
## function activity_sink_set_batch | doc="activity_sink.set — admin-only upsert of one activity_sink card + paired activity_sink_secret row (pgp_sym_encrypt of client_secret with the app.comm_secret_key GUC). Set-based attribute writes via the ordinality-join idiom." | path="functions/activity_sink_set_batch.sql"
## function activity_subscription_set_batch | doc="activity_subscription.set — create / update the CALLER's own notification subscription card under an email activity_sink (title / activity_filter / predicate / rollup_minutes / channel_status). subscriber is always the caller's linked person card; on update the caller must be that subscriber (admins exempt). Only changed attributes write activity rows. A new subscription's activity_sink_state pointer starts at the current max(activity.id) so it never replays history." | path="functions/activity_subscription_set_batch.sql"
## function activity_subscription_delete_batch | doc="activity_subscription.delete — soft-delete the caller's own subscription card (admins exempt) + card_delete activity row." | path="functions/activity_subscription_delete_batch.sql"
## function activity_subscription_list_batch | doc="activity_subscription.list — the caller's own live subscriptions (optionally one project), joined with the parent sink / project / comm channel names and the delivery state row." | path="functions/activity_subscription_list_batch.sql"
## function activity_subscription_sinks_batch | doc="activity_subscription.sinks — the email activity_sinks the caller can subscribe to: live sinks under projects visible to the caller (DI-6 visibility predicate)." | path="functions/activity_subscription_sinks_batch.sql"
## function link_set_batch | doc="link.set — idempotent upsert of a link card (code change / issue / URL) under a task, keyed on (task_id, url): a transaction-scoped advisory lock on the pair serialises concurrent writers, the first call creates the card and repeats PATCH title / link_kind / link_state. Only changed attributes write activity rows, so re-sending an unchanged state is a no-op. Gated on card.update of the parent task." | path="functions/link_set_batch.sql"
## function link_delete_batch | doc="link.delete — soft-delete one link card + card_delete activity row. Gated on card.update of the parent task." | path="functions/link_delete_batch.sql"
## function link_list_batch | doc="link.list — the live links on one task (oldest first) with url / title / kind / state, created_at, updated_at (newest activity on the link) and the creating account's display name. Visibility gated once on the task; an invisible task lists empty." | path="functions/link_list_batch.sql"
## function person_create_batch | doc="person.create — admin-only insert of a global person card with title + person_kind + optional email; tier='user' also provisions a user_account row + user_account_person link." | path="functions/person_create_batch.sql"
## function person_grant_account_batch | doc="person.grant_account — admin-only promotion of an existing person card to a user: mint a user_account + user_account_person link (idempotent if already linked); email from the request override or the person's stored email." | path="functions/person_grant_account_batch.sql"
## function card_access_mint | doc="Make one secret route (card_access row) on a card and return its token once: 20 random bytes as lowercase hex, stored only as its SHA-256. Shared by comm_route.create and calendar_url.create." | path="functions/card_access_mint.sql" | arg_types="bigint, text, text, text, jsonb, text, bigint"
